<a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="2FB0DC"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>Ribosome Profiling </a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="572" name="Google Shape;572;p79"/><p:cNvSpPr txBox="1"/><p:nvPr><p:ph idx="1" type="body"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="320675" y="1295400"/><a:ext cx="4175125" cy="4419600"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln><a:noFill/></a:ln></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr anchor="t" anchorCtr="0" bIns="45700" lIns="91425" numCol="1" rIns="91425" spcFirstLastPara="1" tIns="45700" wrap="square"><a:noAutofit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr algn="l" indent="-342900" lvl="0" marL="342900" marR="0" rtl="0"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPts val="2400"/><a:buFont typeface="Calibri"/><a:buChar char="•"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="2400" u="none"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>It is a method in which a researcher is able to isolate mRNA currently being transcribed. </a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p><a:p><a:pPr algn="l" indent="-342900" lvl="0" marL="342900" marR="0" rtl="0"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="480"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPts val="2400"/><a:buFont typeface="Calibri"/><a:buChar char="•"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="2400" u="none"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>mRNA is isolated and subjected to RNase; only transcripts bound to ribosomes will survive.</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p><a:p><a:pPr algn="l" indent="-342900" lvl="0" marL="342900" marR="0" rtl="0"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="480"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPts val="2400"/><a:buFont typeface="Calibri"/><a:buChar char="•"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="2400" u="none"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>RT-PCR is done and the resultant cDNA is sequenced.</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p><a:p><a:pPr algn="l" indent="-342900" lvl="0" marL="342900" marR="0" rtl="0"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="480"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPts val="2400"/><a:buFont typeface="Calibri"/><a:buChar char="•"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="2400" u="none"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>The data are both quantitative and qualitative.  </a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:cxnSp><p:nvCxnSpPr><p:cNvPr id="573" name="Google Shape;573;p79"/><p:cNvCxnSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvCxnSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="381000" y="914400"/><a:ext cx="8382000" cy="0"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="straightConnector1"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln cap="flat" cmpd="thinThick" w="57150"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="2FB0DC"/></a:solidFill><a:prstDash val="solid"/><a:miter lim="800000"/><a:headEnd len="med" type="none" w="med"/><a:tailEnd len="med" type="none" w="med"/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:cxnSp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr descr="A diagram showing ribosome profiling.
At the top is a large tan oval labeled as cytoplasm. Inside are subunit images, where the large subunit is on bottom. On the left inside the oval are two with a wavy green line extending through them labeled as translation. On the right is a single subunit structure with a wavy green line. Below this is oval is a down arrow indicating where ribosomes and associated mRNAs are isolated. This points to two of the subunits described above, with the green mRNA line. The large subunit is labeled as the ribosome. The left subunit image has a small coiled line coming down and the right one has an even longer blue coil, which represents peptides being synthesized. Below this is a down arrow representing RNase. To the right is a box that states, “Digest unprotected mRNA with RNase. This arrow points to two of the subunit structures, but each of these have their own mRNA lines. Below this is a down arrow to the two green mRNA lines, representing ribosome-protected mRNA segments. To the right of this arrow is a box that states, “Destroy RNase and isolate RNA fragments.” This has a down arrow representing reverse transcriptase (blue). To the right is a box that states, “Make duplex DNA from RNA fragments.” This points to two sets of blue helices, representing duplex DNA. Below this is a box that states, “Deep DNA sequencing reveals mRNA segments undergoing translation.”
